They don't take the vaccine, but then when they get sick, they do come to you at the hospital to get fixed. Yeah, but I think there are a lot of people, though, who have been misled in our country. This is why I don't entirely fault folks themselves for some of these decisions, because if you are consuming a huge amount of misinformation in an echo chamber and are being essentially led to believe that that's all accurate, that's coming from trusted sources, then why wouldn't you think that some of these, COVID's not real, the vaccine's not good for you or some of these other fallacies. So this is why I think also that we have to, if we don't do something about the information environment in which we're operating. And the misinformation.
他们不接种疫苗，但当他们生病时，他们确实会来医院找你治疗。是的，但我认为我们国家有很多被误导的人。这就是为什么我并不完全责怪人们自己做出这些决定，因为如果你在一个回音室里消费了大量的错误信息，并且基本上被引导相信这些都是准确的，这些信息来自可信来源，那么你为什么不认为其中一些，比如新冠不是真的，疫苗对你不好，或者其他一些谬论呢？所以这就是为什么我认为，如果我们不改变我们所处的环境，如果我们不解决错误信息的问题。

